# ─── Secrets. Nothing here may ever be committed. ─────────────────────────────
# This is a public repository. The rule is not "do not commit secrets by
# accident", it is "there is no path by which a secret can reach a commit":
# every file that holds one is named here, and `npm run check:secrets` fails the
# build if any of them appears in the index.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.key
*.pem
config.json
config.local.json
config/
!config.example.json

# Operator-specific data. These carry real phone numbers and message contents,
# which is exactly what a public repo must not hold.
allow.json
blocklist.json
data/
state/

# Every deployment's own .env, config.json, persona and plugin drop-boxes. One
# directory per instance; nothing under it is shareable. See docs/INSTANCES.md.
instances/*
!instances/README.md
# The default instance's plugin drop-boxes. Messages in flight, with numbers in.
plugins/

# ─── Build output and dependencies ────────────────────────────────────────────
node_modules/
dist/
*.tsbuildinfo
coverage/

# ─── Runtime noise ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
*.log
logs/
.DS_Store

# Workspace-local: one contributor's own subagents and settings, tied to their
# own MCP servers. Useful to them, meaningless in a clone.
.claude/
